                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I nearly didnt buy this game because of a negative review by somebody who only played it for 1 hour and when I did get it I wasnt too impressed and wished I'd saved my money. however after looking past the very basic graphics and getting into the gameplay I now think it is a very playable highly tactical game. One of the issues I was struggling with was the controls, everything in the control setup was reffering to aeroplanes and playing this game with keyboard and joystick wasnt right, once I managed to get the gunners station controlled by mouse things took a very different turn and the game became very good, theres nothing as satisfying as destroying an enemy tank while its moving flat out accross your front using old fashioned gunnery techniques ie, no lazer, autolay or computers to help, just get on with it. basically this game is about the gameplay. its very messy setting it up and the basic graphics and sounds can lead you to think its all crap, give it a go, take time to understand it and you will have hours of fun. If you liked M1 Tank Platoon you'll like this",
